  "interpretation": [
    "The record demonstrates two completed fresh FP32 play/update/evaluate cycles with changing LoRA parameters and replayable environments; it does not demonstrate monotonic or unlimited improvement.",
    "All maze training episodes and 15/16 chess training episodes ended under proxy cap rewards; there were no training maze goal finishes or chess checkmates.",
    "Market settlement and controller banked points are actual defined finite-horizon objectives, not substitute end-condition adjudications. Positive relative market reward can coexist with negative absolute PnL.",
    "Historical policies were evaluated, not sampled as training opponents. This is current-self training with historical evaluation, not population-based league training.",
    "Cycle3 fixed-opponent macro return improves over inherited cycle1 but remains slightly below base; three scenario clusters, reused opponents and proxy rewards preclude a robust broad-improvement claim.",
    "Controller feedback improved one of two lineages on untouched seeds; the other remains faulty. Thirty-six of 120 model-peer tournament games are zero-score draws, showing that weak opponents can provide no outcome learning signal.",
    "The controller tournament demonstrates real deterministic execution and some shared-resource competition, not learned weight changes or an automatically growing curriculum."
  ],
